
v0.2.2 (2019-08-28)

 * Add filter for showing information only about devices whose address start
   with given bytes (--filter-partial-addr 0xaabbcc or
   --filter-partial-addr aa:bb:cc)

 * When writing output to UNIX socket, terminate the program if socket is
   closed

v0.2.1 (2019-08-10)

 * Add support for file output (-output-file command line option), which
   allows to write, for example, JSON data into file in a format which is easy
   to parse.

v0.2.0 (2019-04-09)

* Bluewalker can now read ruuvi tag data format 5 as well. The JSON output
  when listening for ruuvi tags has changed to include new fields present
  in v5 data.

* Bluewalker now supports setting random address using -random-addr
  command line option

* Bluewalker can be used to send advertising data. The mode is enabled with
  -broadcast command line option, advertising and scan response data can be
  set with -adv-data and -scan-resp command line options.

* When using filters, packages matching all filters are shown instead of showing
  packets matching any filters. Filters which can have multiple values,
  like address or AD types will match any values. Hopefully this makes
  filtering a bit more intuitive.

v0.1.0 (2019-02-10)

 * Initial tagged version
